  "description": "The proposal comprises the creation of a roof extension, including raising the front and rear ridge heights to match the ridge height and overall volume of No. 58 Cresswell Road, thereby restoring the symmetry of the semi-detached pair, together with increasing the height of the parapet walls to facilitate the infill of the existing butterfly roof slopes.\n\nThe works also involve the construction of a rear dormer with windows facing the rear elevation, and the installation of two rooflights to the front roof slope together with one skylight positioned between the ridges.\n\nThe proposal further includes the insertion of a side-facing second-floor window fitted with obscure glazing and restricted opening, with the opening section positioned at a minimum height of 1.7m above finished floor level.\n\nIn addition, the proposal includes the construction of a single-storey rear extension measuring approximately 2.5m in depth and 3m in height, featuring a flat roof with a 275mm parapet.\n\nAll external materials are proposed to match the existing dwelling.",
